"""Editorial guides for choosing and using this specific collection."""
GUIDES = [
('/italian-anki-decks-for-beginners/', 'Italian Anki Decks for Beginners: Choosing a First Deck',
 'Choose a first Italian Anki deck: compare A1 vocabulary, Fluent Forever, numbers and verb practice, and understand overlap before importing.',
 '''<p>These Italian flashcards are separate downloads, not a sequence you need to finish in order. If you are starting Italian, choose one vocabulary deck, check its sample cards and add specialised practice when you need it.</p>
 <h2>A1 vocabulary or Fluent Forever?</h2>
 <p>The <a href="/decks/italian-cils-a1-anki-deck/">Italian A1 Anki deck</a> follows the CILS A1 word list. It covers vocabulary for family, food, shopping and getting around. Choose it if you want vocabulary organised around a named language level.</p>
 <p>The <a href="/decks/italian-core-fluent-forever-625-anki-deck/">Fluent Forever vocabulary deck</a> is based on Gabriel Wyner’s core word list. Its topics include home, body, food and time. Choose it if you prefer an everyday topic-based starting point. The collection’s deck name refers to the source list; the current downloadable note count is shown on its page.</p>
 <p>Common words occur in both decks. Start with one rather than importing both and assuming every card will be new.</p>
 <h2>Which CILS level should I download?</h2>
 <p>The <a href="/decks/italian-cils-a2-anki-deck/">A2</a>, <a href="/decks/italian-cils-b1-anki-deck/">B1</a> and <a href="/decks/italian-cils-b2-anki-deck/">B2</a> decks include lower-level vocabulary. Choose the level you are currently studying. Importing all four can repeat words and increase your review queue without adding much new material. The <a href="/italian-cils-anki-decks/">CILS levels page</a> compares them side by side.</p>
 <p>A deck’s label describes its vocabulary source, not a promise that finishing the deck gives you that proficiency level. Listening, reading, grammar and conversation still matter.</p>
 <h2>When to add numbers and verbs</h2>
 <p>The <a href="/decks/italian-basics-numbers-anki-deck/">Italian numbers deck</a> focuses on easily confused forms, including teens and tens. Use it if recognising a number takes longer than you want.</p>
 <p>For verbs, start with a tense you are learning in your course or reading. The <a href="/decks/italian-verbs-learning-presente-anki-deck/">presente deck</a> practises forms such as vedo, “I see”. The <a href="/italian-verb-conjugation-flashcards/">verb conjugation overview</a> lists the other tenses and imperative persons. You do not need to import all of them together.</p>
 <h2>Check the card before importing</h2>
 <p>Every deck page includes a real front-and-back sample, a short preview of its contents, card counts and file size. Vocabulary cards generally ask for both recognition and recall; verb and noun-phrase drills ask for the Italian. A note can produce more than one card, so note and card counts differ.</p>
 <p>The pictures, voices and card text are AI-assisted. Listen to the sample and check whether the prompts suit you. If an entry seems wrong, consult a dictionary and edit or suspend it in Anki.</p>
 <h2>A first study session</h2>
 <ol><li>Download one vocabulary deck.</li><li>Open the .apkg file in Anki and check the import summary.</li><li>Choose a modest daily new-card limit, then adjust it as you see your review workload.</li><li>Try to answer before revealing the back. Listen to the recording and say the Italian aloud.</li></ol>
 <p>For practical details, see <a href="/how-to-study-italian-with-anki/">how to study Italian with these Anki flashcards</a>.</p>'''),
('/how-to-study-italian-with-anki/', 'How to Study Italian with Anki Flashcards',
 'A practical guide to importing Italian Anki flashcards, using audio, practising recall, managing overlapping decks and correcting cards.',
 '''<p>These decks are study files for Anki. The website lets you inspect examples and download them; your reviews and scheduling happen in the Anki app.</p>
 <h2>Download and import an Italian deck</h2>
 <p>Choose a deck from the <a href="/#decks">Italian flashcard collection</a>, then download its .apkg file. Pictures and recordings are packaged with the cards. Open the file with Anki, or choose File → Import on a computer. If you already have other decks from this collection, read the import summary rather than assuming that all cards are new.</p>
 <h2>Recall the answer before revealing it</h2>
 <p>For an Italian → English vocabulary card, think of the meaning before looking at the back. For an English → Italian prompt, say or write the Italian first. Revealing the answer immediately can make a card feel familiar without showing whether you can recall it.</p>
 <p>After revealing the back, use Anki’s rating buttons to describe your actual recall. Set a new-card limit that leaves time for reviews; adding every deck at once can create a queue that is difficult to sustain.</p>
 <h2>Study nouns with their articles</h2>
 <p>For a noun such as il caffè, practise the article along with the word. Check the gender and plural details on the answer. The <a href="/decks/italian-noun-phrases-anki-deck/">noun-phrase deck</a> adds practice with articles, possessives and prepositions in phrases such as il loro mondo.</p>
 <h2>Use the audio, then practise listening elsewhere</h2>
 <p>Replay the recording and say the word or phrase aloud. The deck voices are AI-generated; they are pronunciation aids rather than recordings of spontaneous conversation. Use Italian listening material as well, so that you encounter different voices, speeds and contexts.</p>
 <h2>Practise conjugation alongside grammar</h2>
 <p>An English prompt such as “I see” asks for vedo. Learn the pattern and use of the tense alongside the drill. Separate decks cover <a href="/italian-verb-conjugation-flashcards/">present, past, future, conditional and imperative forms</a>; pick the tense that matches what you are studying.</p>
 <h2>Use film examples as context</h2>
 <p>The <a href="/decks/italian-movies-le-otto-montagne-anki-deck/">Le otto montagne</a> and <a href="/decks/italian-movies-benvenuti-al-sud-anki-deck/">Benvenuti al Sud</a> decks include subtitle examples with literal English translations. Word-for-word glosses help connect a word to its sentence, but they may sound unnatural in English. They are not polished subtitle translations.</p>
 <h2>Avoid unnecessary repetition</h2>
 <p>Each CILS level deck includes vocabulary from lower levels. Common words also recur in other vocabulary lists. Choose one level and inspect the contents of any additional deck before importing. If you have already imported overlapping material, review the affected notes in Anki’s browser before deleting anything.</p>
 <h2>Correct or suspend a questionable card</h2>
 <p>These are personal, AI-assisted study materials and can contain mistakes. Check a doubtful definition, gender or form against a dictionary or grammar reference. You can edit the card in Anki, suspend it while you investigate, or <a href="https://github.com/cameronengineer/italian-flashcards/issues">report the problem</a> with the deck name and exact prompt.</p>
 <p>If you are deciding where to start, read <a href="/italian-anki-decks-for-beginners/">choosing an Italian Anki deck for beginners</a>.</p>'''),
]
